  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"6 n equals 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"n equals 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> in the expression <math alttext=\"n plus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"2 plus 4\"><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
